e/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/leetsepeak/dom.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/leetsepeak/dom.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/leetsepeak/dom.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> Covers a lot of the classics, including bottle bugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:16:28-07:00","id":1384855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384825-sesselijae-the-stomach-bottle-bugs-has-anyone-taken-a-shot-at-converting-em?p=1384843#post1384843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/leetsepeak/dom.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/leetsepeak/dom.pdf</a><br /> <br /> Covers a lot of the classics, including bottle bugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several of these demon writeups were plagarized wholesale from Xefas over on the Giantitp forums. You can find the original Aalu, Amphelisiae, Gallmau, Gethin, Heranhal, and Sesseljae <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?457743-Exalted-3e-Xefas-Demonarium-And-Sinister-Laundromat\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:13:30-07:00","id":1385005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384825-sesselijae-the-stomach-bottle-bugs-has-anyone-taken-a-shot-at-converting-em?p=1384855#post1384855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several of these demon writeups were plagarized wholesale from Xefas over on the Giantitp forums. You can find the original Aalu, Amphelisiae, Gallmau, Gethin, Heranhal, and Sesseljae <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?457743-Exalted-3e-Xefas-Demonarium-And-Sinister-Laundromat\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't seem to be plagiarized from Xefas, the descriptive text is significantly different on the few examples I compared and there are minor variations in stat lines (essence costs, dice pools, etc). Are you sure this isn't just a case of having a common parent? These seem to both be useful but distinct resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9011-vaegrim","name":"Vaegrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:51:39-07:00","id":1385013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vaegrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384825-sesselijae-the-stomach-bottle-bugs-has-anyone-taken-a-shot-at-converting-em?p=1385005#post1385005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't seem to be plagiarized from Xefas, the descriptive text is significantly different on the few examples I compared and there are minor variations in stat lines (essence costs, dice pools, etc). Are you sure this isn't just a case of having a common parent? These seem to both be useful but distinct resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that a common parent exists. Xefas wrote her demon writeups in 2015, two years before leetsepeak authored this compilation. The original versions of these demons as they appear in 1e and 2e do not have unique Charm names. It would appear that Charm names in leetsepeak's versions are lifted wholesale. Descriptive text has been changed, but the mechanics of the charms are pretty much identical all the way through.<br /> <br /> For example, with the alternations in bold:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xefas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Form of Creeping, Whistling Doom</b> (5m, 1wp; Simple; Indefinite; Essence 2) When suitably motivated, an Amphelisia may assume a potent combat form. A hidden ruff of webbed skin extends forth from behind their head, and the hum of their essence increases in intensity until it becomes a loud woosh, like a great open flame. Poisonous bugs of all kinds swarm over the Amphelisia and, at the beginning of its next turn, they reach a great enough density that the Amphelisia raises into the air in a vaguely humanoid mass of writhing insects, only its head and ruff visible beneath the grotesque voltron. At the apex of this transformation, the Amphelisia's hum becomes a shrill, piercing whistle that lasts for the duration of the Charm.<br /> <br /> In this form, the Amphelisia gains access to a number of a new Charms, noted below, as well as a new, special health track with three -0 health levels. These levels absorb damage before the demon's normal track, and when they are filled with lethal damage, they disappear along with the damage, and this Charm is forcibly deactivated. Excess damage spills over into the demon's normal health. Furthermore, maintaing this form is taxing to an Amphelisia, and they lose 1 mote of essence at the end of each of their turns in combat, or every minute outside of combat. If they cannot pay this recurring mote cost, the Charm is forcibly deactivated as well. Finally, the Amphelisia gains the Hideous trait while this Charm is active.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Form of Creeping, Whistling Doom (<b>10m</b>, 1wp; Simple; Indefinite; Essence 2): When suitably motivated, an Amphelisia may assume a potent combat form. A hidden ruff of webbed skin extends forth from behind their head, and the hum of their essence increases in intensity until it becomes a loud <b>constant noise</b>, like a great open flame. Poisonous bugs of all kinds emerge from the shadows to swarm over the Amphelisia and, at the beginning of its next turn, they reach a great enough density that the Amphelisia raises into the air in a vaguely humanoid mass of writhing insects, only its head and ruff visible beneath the grotesque voltron. At the apex of this transformation, the Amphelisia\u2019s hum becomes a shrill, piercing whistle that lasts for the duration of the Charm.<br /> <br /> In this form, the Amphelisia gains access to a number of a new Charms, noted below, as well as a new, special health track with <b>four</b> -0 health levels. These levels absorb damage before the demon\u2019s normal track, and when they are filled with lethal damage, they disappear along with the damage, and this Charm is forcibly deactivated. Excess damage spills over into the demon\u2019s normal health.<b> It also gains access to a new weapon, reflecting how its arms become whip-like tentacles of vermin which can lash out at enemies at up to short range. </b>The Amphelisia gains <b>+1 Appearance</b> and the Hideous trait while this Charm is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T23:22:03-07:00","id":1385016,"title":"","content":"Leetsepeak made no secret of the fact that he used some of Xefas's stuff as a base for what he did in demon conversion, but didn't like many of the details in Xefas's versions. Some powers he did like, and used those unchanged, but he significantly modified and added to all of the final demon designs. There wouldn't have been much point in reposting them otherwise, especially considering how up front he was about where he was getting them from.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15BZMrBkO8j_-XZX5030Y0_GNrCvI9JRQhN_uXR-jjsQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1..._uXR-jjsQ/edit</a><br /> <br /> As far as I know, this is a full index of Leetsepeak's demon conversions. Again, you can see that he clearly indicated where he's starting from another person's conversion. Likewise, if you dig up his content hub page here, he definitely mentions Xefas's stuff as being the foundation for some of his final conversions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 05-01-2020, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T23:49:06-07:00","id":1385018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384825-sesselijae-the-stomach-bottle-bugs-has-anyone-taken-a-shot-at-converting-em?p=1385016#post1385016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leetsepeak made no secret of the fact that he used some of Xefas's stuff as a base for what he did in demon conversion, but didn't like many of the details in Xefas's versions. Some powers he did like, and used those unchanged, but he significantly modified and added to all of them. There wouldn't have been much point in reposting them otherwise, especially considering how up front he was about where he was getting them from.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15BZMrBkO8j_-XZX5030Y0_GNrCvI9JRQhN_uXR-jjsQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1..._uXR-jjsQ/edit</a><br /> <br /> As far as I know, this is a full index of Leetsepeak's demon conversions. Again, you can see that he clearly indicated where he's starting from another person's conversion. Likewise, if you dig up his content hub page here, he definitely mentions Xefas's stuff as being the foundation for some of his final conversions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. Glad to know that Xefas is credited on the google doc. There's no mention of that in the pdf, but the credit seems pretty freely given here on the forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}